## Session 145 — wild swing on §D29 — **B-grade case (i)**

Wild-swing target: the discrete-`Z` Cohn-Elkies / Delsarte LP bound on prime autocorrelation. All six default targets in the brief (§C1, §A1, §B1, §A3, §D4, §C2) were already closed in prior sessions, so I picked the highest-A-grade-probability open vector — D29 — re-framed (per agent advice) as a Delsarte LP rather than a literal Cohn-Elkies.

**Both A-grade hypotheses falsified cleanly:**
1. *"Primes saturate the LP within `(log N)^{-c}`"*: FALSE — saturation `S_N` decays as `1/log N` (`{0.835, 0.608, 0.498}` at N=10⁴, 10⁵, 10⁶).
2. *"Optimal `f^*` is a Viazovska modular form"*: FALSE — `f^*(t) ≈ A·cos(πt/2)·1_{t even}`, a trivial period-4 sinusoid reflecting the parity barrier (E2.1).

**B-grade structural finding (new edge E2.23):**
```
f̂*(0; T) ≈ 1.154 + 0.848 · log T   (R² > 0.999, T ∈ {50..1500})
```
Saturation requires `T ≈ N`, placing the LP family **strictly inside the sieve barrier (E6.7)**. The slope 0.85 is a clean structural fingerprint that did not exist in the project before.

